        "image": "as_4x3_oat",
        "heading": "What we do",
        "text": "<p>Larkfield Community Kitchen started in a church hall in 2009 with one soup pot and six volunteers. Today we run a choice pantry, cook a free lunch twice a week and deliver groceries to neighbours who can't get out.</p><p>Anyone who lives in Larkfield or the river villages is welcome. There are no forms, and nobody asks why you came.</p>",
        "link_label": "About us",
        "link": "/about"
      },
